{
	"Name": "AlertQuery - Okta - System - Org - Possible Okta Denial of Service or Rate Limit Abuse [table]",
	"Description": "Counts Okta rate limit warnings and violations. Okta rate-limits per org, so sustained violations either mean an integration has gone into a retry loop or someone is deliberately burning the org's budget to degrade authentication for everyone.\n\nThreshold: 5 or more rate limit events in the window. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/rate-limits/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/",
